# Separate space from physics
@scenario office_lesson_26
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg office]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip desk listen]
pip: A drawing of a desk can look solid while a moving prop passes straight through it.
pip: Open the JES scene in the editor. Plan a collider for the desk and compare it to its visual bounds.
@label check
pip: What determines whether two physical objects can collide?
> Their displayed colors. -> retry
> Their physics bodies and collision shapes. -> correct
@label retry
[show pip desk curious]
pip: Visual bounds and collision shapes serve different purposes. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip desk cheer]
pip: Visual bounds and collision shapes serve different purposes.
> Finish this lesson -> return_hub
> Try the lesson again -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_26]
[flag tutorial_done_26]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_6]
